---
import PiDriveTransfer from "../../layouts/PiDriveTransfer.astro";
---

<PiDriveTransfer
  title="Pi Drive Transfer Privacy Notice - In-Between Labs"
  description="How Pi Drive Transfer accesses Google Drive data, stores personal downloads and OAuth tokens locally, and supports revocation and deletion."
  canonical="https://inbetweenlabs.com/pi-drive-transfer/privacy"
>
  <article class="card p-6 sm:p-8 md:p-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Pi Drive Transfer privacy notice</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-white/60">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-02">October 2, 2026</time></p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-white/70 leading-relaxed">
      <section aria-labelledby="scope-title">
        <h2 id="scope-title" class="text-xl font-semibold text-white/90">Scope and owner</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          This notice applies only to Pi Drive Transfer, Matt Blethen's single-user personal file backup and
          download utility. Matt owns and operates its Google OAuth client and uses the third-party,
          open-source rclone tool on his own Raspberry Pi. It is not a publicly available backup service.
          In-Between Labs' Android apps, including Sigil Synth, are covered by their separate
          <a href="/privacy-policy" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">Android apps privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="data-title">
        <h2 id="data-title" class="text-xl font-semibold text-white/90">Google data accessed and purpose</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The utility connects directly to the Google Drive API using
          <code class="break-all text-white/90">https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly</code>.
          This permission allows it to read and download file contents and metadata, such as file names,
          folder information, sizes, and modification times, across the connected account's Drive.
          The permission is broader than the files selected for a particular download.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Matt uses that access to find and download selected personal files to his own storage for backup
          and local use. This read-only permission does not allow the utility to upload, modify, or delete
          Drive files. Uploads from Matt's separate computer through the official Google Drive desktop app
          are a separate workflow and are not performed by Pi Drive Transfer.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="storage-title">
        <h2 id="storage-title" class="text-xl font-semibold text-white/90">Authorization and local storage</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Authorization is completed with Google through rclone. OAuth access and refresh tokens are
          stored in Matt's local rclone configuration to maintain access for ongoing transfers. The public
          website does not collect Google credentials or OAuth tokens and has no Google Drive sign-in flow.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Downloaded files are stored on Matt's own storage connected to his Raspberry Pi. File contents
          and metadata used during a transfer are processed by rclone on that device. No custom application
          server collects visitors' Drive data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="sharing-title">
        <h2 id="sharing-title" class="text-xl font-semibold text-white/90">Use and sharing</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Google Drive data is used only to carry out this personal download and backup workflow. Transfers
          take place between Google and Matt's own device. The utility does not sell Drive data, share it
          with advertising services, use it to serve ads, or use it to train AI models.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          rclone is third-party software running locally in this setup; it is not a custom service operated
          by this website. Google's handling of data within Google Drive is covered by
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">Google's privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="retention-title">
        <h2 id="retention-title" class="text-xl font-semibold text-white/90">Retention and deletion</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Local copies remain on Matt's own storage until he deletes them. OAuth tokens remain in the local
          rclone configuration for ongoing access until the configuration is removed or the tokens are
          replaced. Matt can stop transfers, delete the downloaded files, and remove the saved rclone
          credentials. There is no public customer account or website-held Drive dataset to delete.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="revoke-title">
        <h2 id="revoke-title" class="text-xl font-semibold text-white/90">Revoking Google access</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The connected account owner can open
          <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">Google Account connections</a>,
          select Pi Drive Transfer, review its access to the Google Account, and remove access. This prevents
          future authorized access to Drive. Revocation does not erase files already downloaded or remove
          token entries from the local rclone configuration; those must be deleted separately on Matt's device.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="website-title">
        <h2 id="website-title" class="text-xl font-semibold text-white/90">Visiting these pages</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          These informational pages do not request access to visitors' Google Drive accounts and include
          no custom analytics or advertising scripts. Website hosting may process standard request
          information, such as IP addresses and browser details, to deliver the pages. Website requests
          are separate from the utility's Drive transfers; Drive files and OAuth tokens are not sent to
          the website by this utility.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="contact-title">
        <h2 id="contact-title" class="text-xl font-semibold text-white/90">Changes and contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          This notice will be updated if the utility's data practices change. The date above identifies
          the current notice. For privacy questions, contact Matt Blethen / In-Between Labs at
          <a href="mailto:inbetweenlabs@gmail.com" class="break-all underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">inbetweenlabs@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <a href="/pi-drive-transfer" class="btn-ghost">Back to Pi Drive Transfer</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</PiDriveTransfer>
